==English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|keh₂p}}
From {{inh|en|enm|upheven}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ūphebban}}, {{m|ang|ūpāhebban||to lift up, raise up, exalt, rise in the air, fly}}, equivalent to {{prefix|up|heave|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|opheffen||to lift, raise}}, {{cog|de|aufheben||to lift, raise, cancel, repeal}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|upheaves|upheaving|upheaved|past2=uphove|upheaved|past_ptc2=uphoven}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[heave]] or [[lift]] up; [[raise]] up or [[aloft]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[lift]] or [[thrust]] something [[upward]] [[forcefully]], or be similarly lifted or thrust upward.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be lifted up; [[rise]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|upheaval}}
* {{l|en|upheaving}}

